{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/881387-partial-hung-in-sunlight-survivable-visible-effects","id":881387,"title":"Partial hung in sunlight survivable? visible effects?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-03T18:08:08-07:00","id":881387,"title":"Partial hung in sunlight survivable? visible effects?","content":"Let's say you secure a vampire in front of a window were only their legs are exposed to sunlight. Let's say it'd be sufficient to burn through their legs. Would it only burn through their legs? would the vampire become a pile of dust and bone completely? would the rest of him catch fire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T20:10:06-07:00","id":881438,"title":"","content":"Providing the sunlight was tightly confined, I'd say it would stop at the legs. At a certain point the legs would be destroyed and no part of the vampire would actually be exposed to the sunlight. Sort of like a specified target attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T04:23:57-07:00","id":881653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/881387-partial-hung-in-sunlight-survivable-visible-effects?p=881438#post881438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Providing the sunlight was tightly confined, I'd say it would stop at the legs. At a certain point the legs would be destroyed and no part of the vampire would actually be exposed to the sunlight. Sort of like a specified target attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't how light works, mind. Light is a wave, if it entered a room it will &quot;spill&quot; all over it, not accounting for the degree that it's absorbed by the materials. <br /> <br /> In 2e it's kinda moot at relatively low BP levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T04:43:11-07:00","id":881662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/881387-partial-hung-in-sunlight-survivable-visible-effects?p=881653#post881653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This isn't how light works, mind. Light is a wave, if it entered a room it will &amp;quot;spill&amp;quot; all over it, not accounting for the degree that it's absorbed by the materials. <br /> <br /> In 2e it's kinda moot at relatively low BP levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Sunlight is not a laser beam :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T04:52:57-07:00","id":881664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/881387-partial-hung-in-sunlight-survivable-visible-effects?p=881653#post881653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't how light works, mind. Light is a wave, if it entered a room it will &quot;spill&quot; all over it, not accounting for the degree that it's absorbed by the materials.<br /> <br /> In 2e it's kinda moot at relatively low BP levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I said if the light was tightly confined. It's the first thing I said. If you just had a regular window, then it wouldn't work, but xenoterracide seemed to have something more specific in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-04-2016, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T05:13:32-07:00","id":881668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/881387-partial-hung-in-sunlight-survivable-visible-effects?p=881664#post881664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why I said if the light was tightly confined. It's the first thing I said. If you just had a regular window, then it wouldn't work, but xenoterracide seemed to have something more specific in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you confine it? if the vampire can <i>see</i> the beam, it's burning the vampire's eyes, even if the primary beam is touching his legs alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T05:38:30-07:00","id":881687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/881387-partial-hung-in-sunlight-survivable-visible-effects?p=881668#post881668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you confine it? if the vampire can <i>see</i> the beam, it's burning the vampire's eyes, even if the primary beam is touching his legs alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall xenoterracide saying the vampire can see the light.<br /> <br /> As for how, it seems to be something members of almost every game can do. Werewolves with Influence, fetishes, spirit allies, I believe there's even some Changing Breeds with powers over sunlight, Mages have Forces and Death, Changelings have Elemental Affinity Contracts, Demons can turn it into a weapon. Then there's the various supernatural entities of the World of Darkness that aren't a played part of their game lines, and of course the stranger Mysterious Places.<br /> <br /> Or you could use an Obfuscate Devotion or a Lancea et Sanctum ritual, maybe a God birthed by Cruac could manage it.<br /> <br /> \u200bPerhaps the Jigsaw-esque designer of such a trap simply <a href=\"http://blog.teachersource.com/2010/07/09/concentrating-sunlight-its-easy/\" target=\"_blank\">looked it up online</a>, allowing for some spillover to catch the rest of the legs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-04-2016, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T06:44:47-07:00","id":881733,"title":"","content":"Vampires don't spontaneously combust or ignite into an inferno and continue to burn when exposed to sunlight in this setting. If they did, damage would be sustained each turn, not in equal amounts over a period of minutes or hours. But it's certainly within the realm of storyteller discretion to describe the damage sustained as a gradually expanding sunburn that blisters the skin, scorch marks, or abrupt flashes of fire that extinguish as quickly as they appear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 05-04-2016, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T07:18:46-07:00","id":881752,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> Focusing light isn't the same as containing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T07:26:42-07:00","id":881764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/881387-partial-hung-in-sunlight-survivable-visible-effects?p=881752#post881752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> Focusing light isn't the same as containing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's some great input, Ephsy. Very helpful. As you no doubt followed the link and saw that the focused light is shining within a dark area, bringing all the light into a sort of beam, your comment has a lot of bearing on nothing I've said.<br /> <br /> To be fair, I am giving xenoterracide the benefit of the doubt. Presumably he has seen windows before, and noticed that they are not surrounded by absolute darkness. It might be unfair to do that, since you were unaware that this question seems to be referencing the Chronicles of Darkness, where so many creatures and objects and things can control sunlight.<br /> <br /> I guess sometimes these things have to be pointed out, like in my posts, where I've covered everything you've so needfully commented on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-04-2016, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T07:47:35-07:00","id":881779,"title":"","content":"You appropriated the example given adding a number of agents that have nothing to do with the scenario proposed. I was simply pointing out that under normal circumstances light isn't a laser. if the subject (ie the vampire) could manipulate light in such a fashion, it would be a non-issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T07:50:27-07:00","id":881782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/881387-partial-hung-in-sunlight-survivable-visible-effects?p=881779#post881779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You appropriated the example given adding a number of agents that have nothing to do with the scenario proposed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I added one. You missed it. 'Providing the sunlight was tightly confined.'<br /> <br /> The other agents were for your benefit, where you seemed to not understand how such a thing could happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T08:46:52-07:00","id":881838,"title":"","content":"Sunlight, under the circumstances described wasn't confined. So your original example bears no point in being addressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T09:01:18-07:00","id":881866,"title":"","content":"I believe the Original Question has been answered.<br /> <br /> Only if the sunlight was CONTAINED in someone way would the legs be the only thing affected. <br /> <br /> Otherwise, the vampire as a whole would take damage as indicated by Humanity and BP until they were completely out of the sun or dead.<br /> <br /> <br /> Circles don't get us anywhere. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T09:05:53-07:00","id":881872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/881387-partial-hung-in-sunlight-survivable-visible-effects?p=881838#post881838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sunlight, under the circumstances described wasn't confined. So your original example bears no point in being addressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The circumstances weren't described very well, were they? You though the vampire was staring at beams of light for some reason.<br /> <br /> If you look <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/881387-partial-hung-in-sunlight-survivable-visible-effects?p=881438#post881438\">here</a> you'll see where I covered it in the first sentence. You understood that a few posts ago, that's why you asked how it was confined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T09:08:58-07:00","id":881875,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">\u200bKnock off the arguing, it isn't productive or useful.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T09:53:36-07:00","id":881925,"title":"","content":"The only way to really contain the sunlight in that way is to put the legs in an opaque box with only the face open to the sun and 2 shrouded holes on top for the legs to enter.<br /> <br /> Or maybe cut 2 holes in the floor and have a window open in the room beneath, although once the legs burn away, the sunlight would eat its away upward if the destroyed flesh fell away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 05-04-2016, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T10:45:13-07:00","id":881971,"title":"","content":"Food for thought, do the legs catch on fire as a side effect of the exposure to sunlight? If the vampire is tied up does it really matter how much sunlight exposure there is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 05-04-2016, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T11:10:41-07:00","id":881995,"title":"","content":"Why would you want to only burn the legs, anyway? Even if you come up with a mechanism to focus the sunlight into a beam and the vampire is restrained, what prevents them from breaking free with Vigor, turning into mist with Protean or commanding you to let them out with Dominate? <br /> <br /> As previously mentioned in this thread, sunlight doesn't really threaten vampires at relatively low Blood Potency/high Humanity. If you want to remove the legs, not even a +3L axe would work, since the damage would be downgraded into bashing and possibly reduced with Resilience. <br /> <br /> This beam of sunlight is sounding like a poorly designed method of torture that won't even do lasting harm, since Vitae can heal all three levels of damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T17:07:59-07:00","id":882358,"title":"","content":"So speaking of Ambient sunlight, how much damage does indirect sunlight do? the book (2e) seems to only talk about the &quot;rays&quot; and running for cover with only eyes exposed... which makes me think that ambient light from the sun is probably not nearly as damaging. if you can't get a sunburn if you lay their all day why would a vamp go crispy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T00:47:10-07:00","id":882645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/881387-partial-hung-in-sunlight-survivable-visible-effects?p=881995#post881995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you want to only burn the legs, anyway? Even if you come up with a mechanism to focus the sunlight into a beam and the vampire is restrained, what prevents them from breaking free with Vigor, turning into mist with Protean or commanding you to let them out with Dominate?<br /> <br /> As previously mentioned in this thread, sunlight doesn't really threaten vampires at relatively low Blood Potency/high Humanity. If you want to remove the legs, not even a +3L axe would work, since the damage would be downgraded into bashing and possibly reduced with Resilience.<br /> <br /> This beam of sunlight is sounding like a poorly designed method of torture that won't even do lasting harm, since Vitae can heal all three levels of damage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Torture is rarely meant for long lasting harm.. it's meant for inflicting pain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T06:55:22-07:00","id":882828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/881387-partial-hung-in-sunlight-survivable-visible-effects?p=882358#post882358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So speaking of Ambient sunlight, how much damage does indirect sunlight do? the book (2e) seems to only talk about the &quot;rays&quot; and running for cover with only eyes exposed... which makes me think that ambient light from the sun is probably not nearly as damaging. if you can't get a sunburn if you lay their all day why would a vamp go crispy?</div> </div> </div> </div>or even if they got crispy it probably would't ash them, like (I forget the characters name) &quot;Mr Crispy&quot; in Blade. I know it's not VtR but I reminded of a level in VtM Redemption where your character has to run from shade to shade in the sunlight. Also movies like blade have deacon frost with makeup and standing in the shade being sufficient, now I think that's a bit out there, but it would seem to enforce the stereotype that it's largely direct sunlight. Unless someone can quote an official reference that it's not just direct sunlight?<br /> <br /> Also in the OP I hadn't really thought about it that much. I had simply thought about my non vampire players discovering bound vampires half ashed by sunlight going through tiny basement windows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 05-05-2016, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T07:17:04-07:00","id":882841,"title":"","content":"Nah, those would be ash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T07:44:20-07:00","id":882863,"title":"","content":"Given that vamipres can avoid taking damage from sunlight by covering up and only leaving their eyes exposed (if low enough BP), I think the discussion has merit. Furthermore, I think this is exactly the kind of thing that the Ordo Dracul would experiment with. I actually can think of some story hooks for it with a really deranged Ordo.<br /> <br /> Personally, if this ever came up in a story... If I was an ST who brought it up, I would have the results be inconclusive depending on the BP/Humanity of the vampire, and &quot;merit further study.&quot; IE - provide a rather deranged and low Humanity antagonistic character. If I was a PC, I would never do it myself, find the entire thing terrible, and act against whomever was doing it. I generally don't play with characters that accept that kind of behavior as the norm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T16:54:55-07:00","id":919379,"title":"","content":"If I were making a torture box to burn off a vampire's legs with sunlight while leaving them alive, I would take the extra time to make the holes you are putting the vampire's bare legs through have an spring-loaded iris aperture with enough pressure to close when the legs had burned away. <br /> <br /> This reminds me of the kind of mindset of the antagonist in <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt1197624/\" target=\"_blank\">Law Abiding Citizen</a> (I am picturing a very angry Hunter who lost their wife and daughter to vampires), or an Ordo Dracul doing some basic testing to create the Scale <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/18795-post-your-scales-of-the-dragon-forum-port#post18795\">SPF 50,000</a> using a vampire she doesn't really like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T17:29:18-07:00","id":920029,"title":"","content":"I believe a mekhet bloodline of 1ed was morevsensitive to sunlight than normal (prob khaibit). I'm pretty sure it was specified they also took some moderate damage from full moon light. I would assume that this is because moonlight is actually just indirect sunlight, so indirect sunlight would be an issue. Now, how much of an issue is it ? One could argue that a mirror is indirect sunlight and mirrored sunlight would kill vampires (I guess everyone would agree on that). On the other hand, an opaque black wall would reflect a lot less light and I don't think both would hurt a vampire as much. There's also the problem of diffraction a ray of light that hits an obstacle rebounds a little in all directions. In that regard, an opaque obstacle would cause a lot more diffraction than a clean mirror (though it would also absord more light). That said, since we're talking about the energy of a unidirectional beam, it would lose a great deal of energy when diffracted and would keep losing energy as you would move away from the spot the beam would hit.<br /> <br /> So now comes the question. Should indirect light matter and to what extend ? I dunno. It's a lot more dramatic if it doesn't and if it's only direct rays and reflected rays (by, say a mirror, a window, a piece of chromed metal...) that hurt the vampire. It means they're safe as long as they manage to get behind an obstacle. It's more cinematic to picture the vampire that just made it behind the door, while the rays dart a few centimeters away from him. Obviously, in the end, it's useless to debate about a precise rule. If it's really ONLY direct and reflected light, then, a vampire could walk in a street as long as they keep in the shade and avoid windows reflections, and that's be stupid.<br /> <br /> Having diffracted, diffuse light kill vampires could add an element of danger, it's not just the rays, but like a wall of hurt that you have to get away from, and a closed room with a sufficiently large window becomes a death trap no matter in what corner you hide. Thing is it'll start getting annoying if you try to get more accurate with that. Whar color are the walls, how opaque, ok, I'm trapped in a room with a window, but the walls are black right ? Even if light fills the place, it's not gonna be nearly as bad as standing in the beam, right ? Then, as a GM, you find yourself tempted to make charts with environment color, opacity and distance from the spot hit by the beam instead of thinking about how to emotionally toy with the PCs and nobody really wins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T21:59:16-07:00","id":920161,"title":"","content":"In common parlance, direct and indirect light have specific meanings. Direct light can be diffused or reflected and remains direct until it becomes indirect. Indirect light is diffuse light which can't be followed back to a source by direct observation. A closed box placed out in the sun with completely opaque walls will have no light within. Poke a hole in the box and a &quot;beam&quot; of light would appear within the box. That beam could be reflected with a mirror or diffused with a crystal to make a larger beam. That would all be direct light. The overall light level within the box would increase because light continues to travel until absorbed. The light level increase outside of the beam would be indirect light. The text is ambiguous as to whether any of that matters. However, moonlight is not a problem so the issue must be from the fact that it is a curse and works via supernatural methods.<br /> <br /> As it is supernatural the laws of nature are not limitations. If a reasonably strong light that comes from the sun during the day falls upon a vampire, I believe it affects a vampire. The text is ambiguous.<br /> <br /> The text is more clear on the damage question originally posed. If only a small part of the body is uncovered then BP is considered one lower than normal. The legs are not small enough so the full effect occurs. Thematically, the legs would appear more damaged and likely tend more to the burning rather than the decaying the rest of the body would like be the reverse. The legs would not get burned off. The final consideration is the legs might be covered with clothing. That should be worth treating like only the eyes uncovered or complete covering depending on the clothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T11:34:35-07:00","id":920466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/881387-partial-hung-in-sunlight-survivable-visible-effects?p=920161#post920161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The text is more clear on the damage question originally posed. If only a small part of the body is uncovered then BP is considered one lower than normal. The legs are not small enough so the full effect occurs. Thematically, the legs would appear more damaged and likely tend more to the burning rather than the decaying the rest of the body would like be the reverse. The legs would not get burned off. The final consideration is the legs might be covered with clothing. That should be worth treating like only the eyes uncovered or complete covering depending on the clothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a particularly disturbing result of the experiment. As such, I like it. Now for our second experiment, lets say we change from dangling legs to merely an exposed hand in that light proof box, with arm and body clamped into place in the dark, of course using a hole you are putting the vampire's bare wrist through have an spring-loaded iris aperture with enough pressure to close if the hand burns away. What would the result be then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-24-2016, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T15:12:29-07:00","id":921189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/881387-partial-hung-in-sunlight-survivable-visible-effects?p=920466#post920466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be a particularly disturbing result of the experiment. As such, I like it. Now for our second experiment, lets say we change from dangling legs to merely an exposed hand in that light proof box, with arm and body clamped into place in the dark, of course using a hole you are putting the vampire's bare wrist through have an spring-loaded iris aperture with enough pressure to close if the hand burns away. What would the result be then?</div> </div> </div> </div>I reference back to the text. The eyes are not burnt away and the vampire no longer takes damage. A high BP vampire would be destroyed from standing out in the sun with only their eyes uncovered. It just takes longer.<br /> <br /> Sunlight is not a weapon. Sunlight is like a bane for ephemeral beings. The sunlight burns away at the essence of what animates a vampire. It is like a mental attack that requires physical contact. It doesn't matter where a person is touched because all parts of the body are connected to the mind.<br /> <br /> If this was a natural phenomenon then eventually the flesh would burn to the point that sunlight could no longer penetrate so the damage would stop. That never happens.<br /> <br /> I think the average surface area of a person is 1.6m^2 for women and 1.9m^2 for men with the surface of the eye area being 3 to 5cm^2. I guess you could reduce the exposed area to a magnitude less of whatever ratio that would be to lower the BP on the damage chart again. Eventually lower BP vampires would not be damaged anymore. Higher BP vampires would be damaged at a slower rate. Dragons probably have figured out exactly how it works out. They might be able to determine exactly how long a particular vampire could burn before destruction and using a small enough iris could prolong it for an entire day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T18:18:57-07:00","id":921266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/881387-partial-hung-in-sunlight-survivable-visible-effects?p=921189#post921189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sunlight is not a weapon. Sunlight is like a bane for ephemeral beings. The sunlight burns away at the essence of what animates a vampire. It is like a mental attack that requires physical contact. It doesn't matter where a person is touched because all parts of the body are connected to the mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Afaik that's not how bane's work for beings like werewolves. Also if that were the case it wouldn't burn a vampire at all, they would simply eventually die. In my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T20:50:57-07:00","id":921329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/881387-partial-hung-in-sunlight-survivable-visible-effects?p=921266#post921266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Afaik that's not how bane's work for beings like werewolves. Also if that were the case it wouldn't burn a vampire at all, they would simply eventually die. In my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves are not ephemeral beings. Look up spirits and ghosts for a more comparable example. Vampires don't always burn. Sometimes they decay and their flesh sloughs off. Burning is when it occurs rapidly for higher BP vampires. Obviously, vampires are not ephemeral either but that is the closest example I can think of to describe what should be happening. A bane damages through symbolic or mystical interference. The moon and sun are different symbols so the same light coming from both affects vampires differently, usually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T22:22:54-07:00","id":921352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/881387-partial-hung-in-sunlight-survivable-visible-effects?p=921329#post921329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves are not ephemeral beings. Look up spirits and ghosts for a more comparable example. Vampires don't always burn. Sometimes they decay and their flesh sloughs off. Burning is when it occurs rapidly for higher BP vampires. Obviously, vampires are not ephemeral either but that is the closest example I can think of to describe what should be happening. A bane damages through symbolic or mystical interference. The moon and sun are different symbols so the same light coming from both affects vampires differently, usually.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the idea of the Bane, simply saying that the bane of silver for werewolves or iron for changelings is probably more comparable. Perhaps I'm wrong though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T05:04:29-07:00","id":921437,"title":"","content":"I'd rule that the exposed part burns off. The bane for ephemeral beings argument is interesting, but I'd argue that Werewolves are about as ephemeral as vampires if not more. They're half spirit, develop bans and can actually sort of ascend to full spirit.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'd rule that vampires being corporal, their banes only affect the exposed body part. It's just more fun and dramatic and opens up potential torture devices with vampires being hung above a sunlight beam by some bond vilain. Something just doesn't feel right about an elder exploding into ashes because he hit his small toe on a sun ray.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T09:34:47-07:00","id":922683,"title":"","content":"I would say both interpretations provide basis for fun and drama.<br /> <br /> The Ephemeral Symbolic Bane argument provides existential dread in its unexpected lack of gore but instead makes the flesh a trap that doesn't burn away to provide relief from the pain of being metaphysically extinguished.<br /> <br /> The Physical Interaction Damage argument does have the gore factor and is fundamentally no different than the fun and drama added by a flamethrower. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}